-- title:
--   Patching datum from a ladder of deformation conditions
-- statement:
--   Fix a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ with finite residue field, a prime (indeed any natural number) $p$ lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, a two-dimensional residual representation $\bar\rho$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over the residue field of $\mathcal O$ factoring through a finite level, and $n\in\mathbb N$. The data are: a family $\mathcal D(k)$ of deformation conditions, each a predicate on rank-two adically continuous Galois representations over local $\mathcal O$-algebras, monotone in the sense that for $k<n$ every representation of type $\mathcal D(k+1)$ is of type $\mathcal D(k)$; for each $k$ a complete noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra $T_k$ that is finite free as an $\mathcal O$-module with local structure map, a representation $\rho_{T_k}$ over $T_k$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi_{T_k}:T_k\to\mathcal O$ whose kernel satisfies, for $k\le n$, that the image under $\pi_{T_k}$ of the annihilator of $\ker\pi_{T_k}$ is nonzero; and a $T_k$-module $M_k$, finite free over $\mathcal O$, with an $\mathcal O$-bilinear pairing $B_k$ which for $k\le n$ is $T_k$-self-adjoint and induces a bijection onto the $\mathcal O$-dual, whose $\ker\pi_{T_k}$-torsion submodule is nonzero and satisfies $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O}M_k=\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O}(M_k[\ker\pi_{T_k}])\cdot\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O}T_k$. Here a `DeformationRingData` for $\mathcal D$ consists of a complete noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra $R$ with residue field that of $\mathcal O$, together with an absolutely irreducible $\bar\rho$ and a representation $\rho$ over $R$ of type $\mathcal D$ with residual representation $\bar\rho$, universal for local $\mathcal O$-algebra maps up to equivalence. At the top rung it is assumed that every such datum $D$ for $\mathcal D(n)$ admits a surjective local $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:D.R\to T_n$ carrying $D.\rho$ to $\rho_{T_n}$, and that for every local $\varphi:D.R\to T_n$ realising $\rho_{T_n}$ there are $r$ and a patching datum over $\mathcal O$ with parameters $p,r$ for $D.R$ acting on $M_n$ through $\varphi$ (a `PatchingDatum` being, for each $m$, a level-$m$ presentation of a module over $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$ modulo the ideal generated by the $(1+X_j)^{p^m}-1$). For each $k<n$ the rung hypotheses are: a datum for $\mathcal D(k+1)$ exists; every datum for $\mathcal D(k)$ maps surjectively and locally onto $T_k$ realising $\rho_{T_k}$; there are a nonzero $c\in\mathcal O$, $\mathcal O$-linear maps $i:M_{k+1}\to M_k$ and $j:M_k\to M_{k+1}$ adjoint for the pairings, and $\Delta\in T_{k+1}$ with $j\circ i=\Delta\cdot$, $(\pi_{T_{k+1}}\Delta)=(c)$ as ideals, and $i$ carrying the $\ker\pi_{T_{k+1}}$-torsion of $M_{k+1}$ onto the $\ker\pi_{T_k}$-torsion of $M_k$; and for all data $D_0$ for $\mathcal D(k+1)$, $D'$ for $\mathcal D(k)$ and local $\varphi_0:D_0.R\to T_{k+1}$ realising $\rho_{T_{k+1}}$, every local $\theta:D'.R\to D_0.R$ carrying $D'.\rho$ to $D_0.\rho$ satisfies the cotangent bound $\operatorname{length}_{\mathcal O}\ker(\pi_{T_{k+1}}\varphi_0\theta)^{\mathrm{cot}}\le\operatorname{length}_{\mathcal O}\ker(\pi_{T_{k+1}}\varphi_0)^{\mathrm{cot}}+\operatorname{length}_{\mathcal O}\mathcal O/(c)$, and any local $\varphi':D'.R\to T_k$ realising $\rho_{T_k}$ satisfies $\pi_{T_k}\circ\varphi'=\pi_{T_{k+1}}\circ\varphi_0\circ\theta$. The conclusion: for every datum $D$ for $\mathcal D(0)$, every representation $\rho'$ over $T_0$ of type $\mathcal D(0)$ whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along the induced residue field map and which is realised by some surjective local map from $D.R$, and every local $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi:D.R\to T_0$ carrying $D.\rho$ to $\rho'$, there exist a nontrivial abelian group $M_x$ with compatible $D.R$- and $T_0$-module structures, the $D.R$-action being that obtained through $\varphi$, and an $r\in\mathbb N$ for which a patching datum $\mathcal O$, $p$, $r$, $D.R$, $M_x$ exists.
--
--   This is the inductive spine of the Taylor–Wiles ladder: it propagates, down a finite chain of successively weaker deformation conditions, the existence of a patching datum together with the identification of the deformation ring with the Hecke algebra, from the top rung (where the Taylor–Wiles input is assumed) to the foot. It is invoked in the Hecke-algebra applications that establish bijectivity of the map from the deformation ring and the complete-intersection presentation in the level-lowering steps of the proof of Fermat's Last Theorem.
